        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0004"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0004",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0005"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0005",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0006"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0006",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0007"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0013-l0000",
      "p0001-n0013-l0001",
      "p0001-n0013-l0002",
      "p0001-n0013-l0003",
      "p0001-n0013-l0004",
      "p0001-n0013-l0005",
      "p0001-n0013-l0006",
      "p0001-n0013-l0007"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "In TASK 2 & 3: First, we use Cosine similarity and Euclidean similarity to measure global similarity Sglobal and local similarity Spart in two aspects of music, and consider the in\ufb02uence of popular trends to build Multi-dimensional music similarity evaluation model to measure the similarity of music (MS). Music within genres is found to be more similar than between genres. Then, to investigate the distinguishing features of genres, we combine different features and built the Discrimination evaluation model of feature combination to select the feature combinations that better distinguish genres from each other. Finally, we analyze changes in genres over time."
  },
  {
